            <ArticleTitle>[Adenocarcinoma of the small intestine. A case report and the clinico-therapeutic considerations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adenocarcinoma of the small bowel is a rare tumor. The diagnosis is often tardy and surgical treatment is still palliative in most cases. A major interest toward this kind of tumor as well as an early diagnosis may give the opportunity to perform a radical operation allowing better results in terms of survival.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
